Experiment 45: To Capture a Screenshot of a Web Page and Store It in the Local System Using Selenium WebDriver

AIM
To write a Selenium WebDriver program to capture a screenshot of a web page and save it in the local system.

ALGORITHM
1. Start the program.
2. Launch the Chrome browser using Selenium WebDriver.
3. Open the required website.
4. Maximize the browser window.
5. Capture the screenshot using the `TakesScreenshot` interface.
6. Save the screenshot in the local system using `FileHandler.copy()`.
7. Display the screenshot saved message.
8. Close the browser.

## CODE

**File name: `ScreenshotTest.java`**

```java
import org.openqa.selenium.WebDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.chrome.ChromeDriver;
import org.openqa.selenium.OutputType;
import org.openqa.selenium.TakesScreenshot;
import org.openqa.selenium.io.FileHandler;
import org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;
import java.io.File;
import java.io.IOException;

public class ScreenshotTest {

    @Test
    public void captureScreenshot() throws IOException {

        WebDriver driver = new ChromeDriver();

        driver.get("https://www.google.com");

        driver.manage().window().maximize();

        File source = ((TakesScreenshot) driver)
                .getScreenshotAs(OutputType.FILE);

        File destination = new File("screenshot.png");

        FileHandler.copy(source, destination);

        System.out.println("Screenshot captured successfully.");
        System.out.println("Saved as: screenshot.png");

        driver.quit();
    }
}
```

## INPUT
- Website: https://www.google.com
- Browser: Google Chrome
- Screenshot file name: `screenshot.png`

## EXPECTED OUTPUT

```text
Screenshot captured successfully.
Saved as: screenshot.png
```

## RESULT
Thus, the screenshot of the web page was captured and stored successfully in the local system using Selenium WebDriver.
